# ISSUE.log

Running log of known defects, gaps, and deferred decisions for Save Philly Festivals.
Newest first. Each entry records what is wrong, why it matters, and what closes it.

Status values: OPEN | IN PROGRESS | RESOLVED | DEFERRED | WONTFIX

---

## 2026-08-10 — Geocoding fallback can't help venue-only locations with no comma
**Status:** RESOLVED — interactive address confirmation shipped on both the producer and admin sides
**Severity:** Low-medium — cosmetic (missing map pin), not a data-integrity issue
**Area:** `src/features/festivals/geocoding-service.js`, `location-lookup-schema.js`,
`LocationLookupPanel.jsx`, `useLocationLookup.js`, `producer-submission-http.js`, `editorial-http.js`

Investigated a missing map pin on "South Philly Caribbean Festival"
(`c1919f87-b157-4878-b22c-e2673689bff0`, `location: "9th Street Italian Market"`,
`geocode_status: failed`, `geocode_failure_reason: no_match`, 3 attempts). Confirmed this is one
instance of the already-known, already-quantified gap: 238/415 festivals resolved, 87 failed
(54 `no_match`, 31 `unmappable_location`, 2 `outside_region`), 90 never attempted (no location
text) — matches the 238/415 (57%) figure already in `Known-Issues.md`.

Root cause: `buildFallbackQuery()` only retries when the raw `location` text has 2+ comma-separated
segments, so it can drop the leading one ("Venue, 123 Street Ave" → retries as "123 Street Ave").
**14 of the 54 `no_match` festivals have a comma-less, venue-only location and never got a fallback
attempt at all** — including this one, "Mann Center Summer Music Festival" →
`"The Mann Center for the Performing Arts"`, and "Philly Taco Challenge" → `"Xfinity Live!"`.
Rerunning `festival-geocode.mjs apply` kept producing the same result no matter how many times it
ran, since there was no second query to fall back to.

**Closed by:** a shared, human-in-the-loop address confirmation step, per the discussion that the
legacy-imported backlog has no producer (`festival-import-repository.js` never sets
`submitted_by`) so an admin-only fix wouldn't reach the 87-festival backlog's root cause, while a
producer-only fix wouldn't touch the backlog. Built both, sharing one service:

- `geocoding-service.js` gained `searchLocationCandidates()` — a single, human-triggered Nominatim
  lookup (limit 5, same region/precision filtering as `classifyGeocodeResult`) that returns
  candidate matches instead of writing anything. Same "singular, triggered by a person, not a
  batch" reasoning that already made the on-demand `geocodeFestival` button acceptable inline.
- New shared request schema: `location-lookup-schema.js`.
- Two new POST endpoints, each behind that area's existing authorization/origin/rate-limit gate:
  `/api/producer/festivals/location-lookup` (`authorizeProducer`, new `location_lookup: 20/min`
  bucket in `producer-request-security.js`) and `/api/admin/festivals/location-lookup`
  (`authorizeEditor`, existing `mutationGate`).
- Shared client hook (`useLocationLookup.js`) and UI (`LocationLookupPanel.jsx`, "Find address" →
  pick a candidate → "Use this address") mounted under the location field in both
  `ProducerSubmissionEditor.jsx` (new submissions, so bad addresses stop entering the pipeline at
  the source) and `AdminFestivalEditor.jsx` (covers the legacy backlog and gives editors an
  override during review).
- Deliberately writes only the `location` text, never coordinates — the geocode sweep / existing
  "Geocode now" button stay the only writer of `latitude`/`longitude`, so this doesn't introduce a
  second write path that could disagree with the sweep.

Verified: `tests/unit/geocoding-service.test.js` covers candidate filtering (drops
state/country-level and out-of-region results), the unmappable-location short-circuit (no request
sent), and provider-failure handling. Lint and `tsc --noEmit --project jsconfig.json` are clean on
every touched file. Full suite run via the documented direct-vitest fallback
(`cd apps/save-philly-festivals && ../../node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config vitest.config.js`):
313 passed, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure (a Windows path-separator bug in
`tests/unit/uploads.test.js`, backslash vs forward-slash, not touched by this change).

**Not fixed as part of this:** the existing 87 already-failed legacy festivals still need someone
to open each one in the admin editor and click through the new panel — this ships the tool, not a
bulk backfill. Running `pnpm exec nx run save-philly-festivals:test` (the Nx-wrapped target, as
opposed to direct vitest) currently fails all 45 test files with
`Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'config')`, reproducible before this change too —
looks like an Nx/vitest version-wiring issue unrelated to this feature; flagging here rather than
fixing it, since diagnosing the Nx plugin/vitest 4.x mismatch is a separate task.

