## 2026-08-10 — Verified: "approved" ≠ "published" is real and already documented correctly
**Status:** RESOLVED (verified, not a bug — no doc change needed)
**Severity:** N/A
**Area:** `prisma/schema.prisma` (`FestivalWorkflowState`), `docs/Client-Call-Walkthrough-Script.md`

Checked whether an approved festival still needs a separate publish step, and whether that's
disclosed to the client. `FestivalWorkflowState` has `approved` and `published` as distinct,
sequential states, and `publication-policy.js` gates public visibility on `published` only —
`approved` festivals stay private. `Client-Call-Walkthrough-Script.md` Phase 3 already states this
explicitly: "notice approval and publication are separate steps — approving registers editorial
acceptance while keeping the festival private, so you can preview before it goes live." No change
made.

