## 2026-08-10 — Signed-in `public` users cannot reach their application status
**Status:** RESOLVED 2026-08-10
**Severity:** High — blocks the producer onboarding flow end to end
**Area:** `src/components/shared/NavBar.jsx`

**What's wrong**
`/account` correctly tracks a producer-access application (pending → "Awaiting review",
rejected → shows the decision reason and allows reapplying, approved → "Producer access
active"). The page works. It is simply unreachable through the UI.

`NavBar` computes `isStaff` and `isProducer` and renders the email chip and Sign Out button only
when `(isStaff || isProducer)`. A self-registered user holds the `public` role by design —
signup grants nothing, and producer access is approved separately — so that user sees a "Login"
button while already signed in, gets no Sign Out control, and has no link to `/account`.

**Why it matters**
This is the exact person the page exists for. Someone who signs up and requests access has no
way to check on it short of typing the URL, and the nav actively tells them they are logged out.
It makes a working feature look broken.

**Fixed by**
`NavBar` now derives `isSignedIn` from the session rather than from the role, shows a "My account"
link to `/account`, and gates the email chip and Sign Out on it. Applied to both the desktop nav
and the mobile disclosure menu. `isStaff`/`isProducer` still drive the portal links, so a
`public` user correctly sees no admin or producer portal.

Verified: signed-out visitors still see only "Login" and no account link; lint, 336 unit tests,
and the production build all pass.

