## 2026-08-10 — QA verification account exists on the production database
**Status:** RESOLVED (mitigated; row is permanent)
**Severity:** Low
**Area:** `User` table

`qa-producer-flow@example.test` was created while verifying the producer-access flow against the
production database and was briefly an active producer account. `UserAccountTransition` rows are
append-only by database trigger, so the user cannot be deleted. It has been deactivated
(`status: deactivated`, revision 2) and `src/lib/auth.js` authenticates only `status === "active"`
users, so it cannot sign in. It will remain visible in Admin → Settings.

