## 2026-08-10 — Account emails and organizer emails share one provider
**Status:** RESOLVED (by design, documented here so it is not "simplified" later)
**Severity:** Critical if regressed
**Area:** `src/features/producer-access/producer-access-notifications.js`

Producer-access decision emails and festival workflow notifications both send through Resend.
Festival notifications are addressed to organizer contact details imported from the source
spreadsheet — people who never signed up for anything — and there are ~1,600 outbox rows waiting.

Account emails are therefore gated on their own switch, `ACCOUNT_EMAILS_ENABLED`, in addition to
`RESEND_API_KEY`. Setting the API key alone must never arm organizer email. Do not "simplify"
this by keying account email off the presence of the API key.

Mitigating fact, verified: there is no bulk notification sweeper, so a key alone would not drain
the backlog. Delivery happens inline during an admin transition or via the one-at-a-time retry
button.

